Sums a list of integers. A list is a chain of pairs ending in nil, and (@ l) is 1 for nil. head and tail give a Result, so the sum is a Result: the base case tests for nil before taking the head.
---

---
letrec total = fn l (if (= (@ l) 1)
	(Ok 0)
	(let h = (head l)?
	let t = (total ((tail l)?))?
	Ok (+ h t)))
total
---
~ => Ok 0 fuel 100000
[1 2 3] => Ok 6 fuel 100000
[5 -2 10] => Ok 13 fuel 100000
